# Renamed to .gitignore by `create`; a package drops dotfiles named .gitignore.
#
# No trailing slash: a symlinked node_modules (a linked local dependency) is not
# a directory, and `node_modules/` would let the link be committed.
node_modules

# The build. Made on the machine that runs it (`bun run build`, which a host runs
# when it installs or updates this module), stamped with the commit, and served
# by `serve.ts` only while that stamp is the checkout's HEAD. A checked-in copy
# would be a second answer to "what does this page say", which disagrees with the
# first the moment somebody edits `src/`.
dist

# Written by `build.ts` for the length of a build and taken away after. Left
# behind by a killed build, it would be what Vite answers at `/`, with no
# ticket in it.
/index.html
